# Katmate OS — netVM sysVM package manifest (ADR-021)
# One package per line. '#' comments and blank lines ignored.
# Installed with --no-install-recommends, so list what is actually needed.

# --- kernel (stock Debian; exported host-side, boots via -kernel/-initrd) ---
linux-image-amd64
initramfs-tools
# cpio: required by initramfs generation. initramfs-tools normally pulls it,
# but --no-install-recommends can drop it — list it explicitly so the kernel
# postinst's initrd generation cannot fail on a missing tool.
cpio
# zstd: initramfs-tools compresses with zstd when the binary is on its PATH and
# silently falls back to gzip when it is not, logging "No zstd in <PATH>, using
# gzip" and recording the choice nowhere else. Measured 2026-09-03: zstd was
# absent from the image (dpkg: "unknown ok not-installed"), so the initrd that
# shipped was gzip-compressed.
#
# The property wanted here is NOT gzip or zstd. It is that the compressor is
# CHOSEN rather than inherited from whatever happens to be installed. Absence
# is a fragile way to choose: the first package that ever pulls zstd in flips
# the initrd's compression with no line in the manifest changing and no field
# in the meta recording it. Same shape as waypipe's `auto` features resolving
# to lz4:false against whatever libs the build host had (ADR-008 gotcha 2,
# ARCHITECTURE.md § Guest waypipe build 2) — which is why those are forced to
# `enabled` rather than left to resolve.
#
# Takes effect at the next netVM rebuild; it changes the artefact, not the
# build's behaviour.
zstd

# --- NIC firmware (the last uplink blocker, 2026-07-08: rtl8125b-2.fw) ------
firmware-realtek

# --- networking core --------------------------------------------------------
# dhcpcd holds the uplink's lease and writes /etc/resolv.conf (ADR-037 R6).
# systemd-networkd still ships with systemd but is disabled in netVM (R15).
# `dhcpcd`, not `dhcpcd-base` alone: dhcpcd-base carries the daemon and hooks
# but no unit; dhcpcd adds dhcpcd.service and depends only on dhcpcd-base and
# sysvinit-utils (Essential). Neither pulls dbus or libdbus by Depends: (trixie,
# 1:10.1.0-11+deb13u4; R16). Its sandbox cannot CREATE /etc/resolv.conf, only
# rewrite it, so build/netvm.sh bakes an empty one (R29).
dhcpcd
nftables
iproute2

# --- VPN --------------------------------------------------------------------
wireguard-tools

# --- console / diagnostics (dev; trim for release) --------------------------
# Keep minimal — netVM is the most exposed VM. Add only what debugging needs.
iputils-ping
